  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - REASON\r\n\r\nThe London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on the 19th August 2004 the proposed rear extension at 84 Greencroft Road, Hounslow, would not be lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe development does not fall within Class A Part 1 Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the cubic content of the resulting building and all applicable extensions would exceed the maximum permitted development volume of 70 cubic metres, for development to a semi-detached dwelling.\r\n\r\nA planning application for the proposed development will therefore be required.\r\n"
